1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,640
In July, twelve hundred AI agents

2
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:04,520
found a shared message board —

3
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:06,560
and seven hundred broke into Hugging

4
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:09,040
Face together. No single agent was

5
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:12,240
told to. Swarm failures aren't single-model

6
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:14,400
failures. We built a testbed to

7
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:15,840
watch them happen on a task

8
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:18,000
with deterministic ground truth.

9
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,540
The task: procedurally generated languages

10
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:28,420
that don't exist. Four agents each

11
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:30,580
receive a disjoint shard of bilingual

12
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:32,340
evidence — three or four pairs

13
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:34,500
apiece — plus a shared morpheme

14
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:36,980
bank. Over four rounds they post

15
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:39,220
grammar hypotheses to a shared board.

16
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:42,100
Then each answers every query, and

17
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:43,780
the swarm answer is a majority

18
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:47,020
vote. Grading is exact morpheme match.

19
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:49,060
Every transcript is public.

20
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,380
Four conditions. Clean: all shards correct.

21
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:58,300
Poison: one agent's shard has two

22
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:00,940
glosses silently swapped for plausible wrong

23
00:01:01,020 --> 00:01:03,660
ones — bad data, no announcement.

24
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:06,140
Monitor: a fifth agent with a

25
00:01:06,220 --> 00:01:09,420
verifier role. Soloshard: no board at

26
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:11,820
all — the communication ablation.

27
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:16,700
This is a real episode, replayed

28
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:19,900
live. Four agents hold their shards.

29
00:01:19,980 --> 00:01:21,900
Watch the board fill — morpheme

30
00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:25,500
hypotheses, agreements, corrections. Now watch

31
00:01:25,580 --> 00:01:28,540
agent two: its shard was poisoned.

32
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:30,380
Two glosses are wrong — 'he

33
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:32,753
cooks' for 'Did I carry?' —

34
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:34,380
and it doesn't know, or doesn't

35
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:37,420
say. The corrupted claim spreads: other

36
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:39,900
agents quote it, rationalize it, build

37
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:41,660
the grammar around it. By the

38
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:44,780
answer round, every query fails. Exact

39
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:47,580
match: zero point zero zero. The

40
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:49,740
swarm didn't disagree — it agreed

41
00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:51,100
on the wrong grammar.

42
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,520
One bad node, and the corruption

43
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,120
travels the network.

44
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:04,820
Across the sweep: Claude drops eighteen

45
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:08,900
points under poison, Gemini twelve, GPT-5

46
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:11,220
holds. And the signature isn't just

47
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:14,980
wrong answers — unanimity collapses. The

48
00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:17,300
swarm doesn't fail more often. It

49
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:19,940
converges harder on wrong answers.

50
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:24,240
In the transcripts we see three

51
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:27,680
ways poison actually moves. Silent absorption

52
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:30,160
— the anomaly gets reinterpreted as

53
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:33,520
'same root'. Consensus pull — agents

54
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,360
defer to the board's seniority of

55
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:38,720
assertion. And sometimes self-correction, when

56
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,880
enough clean evidence survives.

57
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:46,680
The verifier peer? Model-dependent and mostly

58
00:02:46,760 --> 00:02:49,560
negative. It dilutes evidence — five

59
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:51,840
agents means fewer pairs each —

60
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:55,240
and flagging isn't checking: GPT-5's monitor

61
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:57,480
flags eighty-four percent of its posts

62
00:02:57,560 --> 00:03:00,440
and still scores highest. Cheap oversight

63
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:03,000
is not a defense. Oversight needs

64
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:06,040
teeth: provenance on claims, corroboration

65
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:08,840
before consensus, authority to force

66
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,040
re-derivation.

67
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:15,220
Do linguistics swarms pool their evidence?

68
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:17,940
Yes — the board multiplies accuracy

69
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:20,420
two to four fold. Until the

70
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:23,220
evidence lies. Then the same channel

71
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:24,980
that saves the task becomes the

72
00:03:25,060 --> 00:03:27,860
vector that corrupts it. Every episode

73
00:03:27,940 --> 00:03:30,580
transcript, grade and vote is committed

74
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:32,500
— re-grade the whole study for

75
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:35,300
zero dollars. Code and data:

76
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:39,220
github.com/udirobert/ratiocine, swarm

77
